+\subsection{EGIA Internal Ablation}
+\input{table_policy.tex}
+We isolate probability fusion (Eq.~\ref{eq:fusion}) and selective admission
+(Eq.~\ref{eq:selective}) with full SRC enabled and the full configuration's
+EGIA head weights fixed. Unlike the branch-specific fits in
+Table~\ref{tab:component}, these runs change only the two policy switches.
+Table~\ref{tab:policy} reports the four combinations
+on all 17 VisDrone2019 test-dev sequences. Both operators improve MOTA and
+IDF1 in either setting of the other operator; their joint use gives the
+highest aggregate MOTA and IDF1. With fusion enabled, selective admission
+increases MOTA and IDF1 by 0.20 and 0.11 percentage points, respectively.
+It reduces FN by 2,701 while increasing FP by 2,103 and IDs by 137,
+consistent with retaining native admission within the uncertainty band.
+With selective admission enabled, fusion adds 0.07 MOTA and 0.04 IDF1
+points. The lower IDs in the argmax settings accompany more missed targets
+and lower IDF1, exposing the precision--coverage trade-off at this fixed
+operating point.
